 "description": "The Cr50 U2F Cryptographic Library is a firmware-hybrid module residing in the Google, LLC Google Security Chips (GSC) chip. The module is responsible for low-level cryptographic primitives on Google Security Chips (GSC) used in recent versions of Google Chromebooks, and includes functionality for key generation, signature generation, random bit generation, keyed-hashing and signature verification operations in support of U2F-related requests in the Cr50 Chrome OS.",
